        "id": "p37-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$28x^4y+64x^3y-60x^2y$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4x^2y(7x-5)(x+3)$\n\nTake out the common factor, then split the middle term and group.",
          "worked": "Since $21\\times(-5)=-105$ and $21-5=16$,\n$$\\begin{align*}28x^4y+64x^3y-60x^2y&=4x^2y(7x^2+16x-15)\\\\28x^4y+64x^3y-60x^2y&=4x^2y(7x^2+21x-5x-15)\\\\28x^4y+64x^3y-60x^2y&=4x^2y\\bigl(7x(x+3)-5(x+3)\\bigr)\\\\28x^4y+64x^3y-60x^2y&=4x^2y(7x-5)(x+3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2p^2-8y^2p^2-4x^2q^2+32y^2q^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(p+2q)(p-2q)(x+2\\sqrt{2}y)(x-2\\sqrt{2}y)$\n\nGroup to obtain two differences of squares, then factorise both.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2p^2-8y^2p^2-4x^2q^2+32y^2q^2&=p^2(x^2-8y^2)-4q^2(x^2-8y^2)\\\\x^2p^2-8y^2p^2-4x^2q^2+32y^2q^2&=(p^2-4q^2)(x^2-8y^2)\\\\x^2p^2-8y^2p^2-4x^2q^2+32y^2q^2&=(p+2q)(p-2q)\\bigl(x^2-(2\\sqrt{2}y)^2\\bigr)\\\\x^2p^2-8y^2p^2-4x^2q^2+32y^2q^2&=(p+2q)(p-2q)(x+2\\sqrt{2}y)(x-2\\sqrt{2}y)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
